            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and evaluation of coumarin derivatives against human lung cancer cell lines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e6455</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0100-879X2017001100603</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/1414-431X20176455</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Series of novel coumarin derivatives [I (a-d) and II (a-d)] were successfully synthesized and their structures were determined based on infrared 1H-nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR), HRMS, and single crystal X-ray crystallography. Additionally, the new synthesized compounds were evaluated to identify the molecular characteristics that contribute to their cytotoxicity, which was tested against SK-LU-1, SPC-A-1 and 95D human lung cancer cell lines, using the MTT assay. The results of this study showed that compounds Ic, Id, IIc, and IId exhibited an efficient percentage of inhibition of cell proliferation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
